{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547213-limbus-company-s-lamacha-clan-in-the-context-of-vtm","id":1547213,"title":"Limbus company's Lamacha Clan In the Context of VtM.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-24T02:23:32-08:00","id":1547213,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Limbus company's Lamacha Clan In the Context of VtM.","content":"What it says on the tin, really.<br /> <br /> Now to provide a bit of context Limbus company is a South Korean gacha game that well regarded for it's character focused narrative centered around it's main cast which are collectively called Sinners who happen to be named after classic literary characters (ex: Ishmel- Main POV character of Moby dick, Heathcliff- The protagonist turned antagonists in Withering Heights, Gregor-The guy who was turned into a bug in The Metamorphosis, and Don Quixote- The minor noble turned knight cosplayer in his titular novel Don Quixote), with each chapter (or canto) focus on a individual sinner. The latest released Canto as of writing this is focused on Don Quixote and her relationship to the bloodfiends inhabiting a runed amusement park called LaMacha Land.<br /> <br /> Now Bloodfiends are to put it simply VtM Vampires on all but name. Like seriously They're call each other kindreds, the lower generation is stronger than the higher ect. One could even argue that the &quot;Hardblood Arts&quot; they use could count as a Discipline that's kind of like Vicissitude though it's focused on manipulating and transmuting blood into different materials rather than body modifications. We even see various level of the Discipline, from the low dot users only capable of crystalizing blood into crude weapons to higher dots being able to create weapons that they could reshape on a whim and finally the clans's Antivuillean is able to create a whole Amusement Park that they have some measure of control over like a vampiric Fisher King.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the Antivuillean his story is quite fascinating.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Basically he has undergone Golconda like Saulot though unlike Saulot he has stayed with his clan intending to guide them to follow his dream of equality with humanty. Unfortunately due to a combination of him totally underestimating his kindred's need for blood and feelings of parental intense parental neglect (The Bloodfiend clans has a heavy familial theme with they Antivuillean viewed as Mother or Farther of the clan as a whole) that lead the clan to plotting against they Antivuillean and leading to chaotropic series of eventsthat ended with the whole theme park along side nearly whole LaMacha Clan (besides one exception) sealed away for 200 years.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder how well the above would translate into VtM...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 12-24-2024, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T17:52:25-08:00","id":1547227,"title":"","content":"Disciplines: Celerity, Fortitude, Hardblood<br /> <br /> Clan Weakness: Members of the Clan suffer from Rotschreck when seeing (or when exposed to) water, in equivalent amounts to fire.<br /> <br /> Seems simple enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T19:08:28-08:00","id":1547229,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat familiar with the Limbus' setting through friends though i've never played it.<br /> <br /> Though i feel the scale and niche of their narrative (plus, their founder's power and the amusement park storyline feels like something that would fit in the 7-8 powers ballpark, imho) mesh better with a bloodline than a clan per se, yes, the LaMancha bloodfiends would fit well enough in VtM overall. In fact i would be mighty tempted to connect their Founder with either Golconda and ideas of Transcedence through the Inconnu, the Brujah's idealized concept of Carthage as an attempt at human-kindred utopia without Masquerade/Silence of Blood or both things even.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents of thought and feel free to twist or ignore anything as the mood suits you.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}